# A1 form-item requirement confirmation

Lesson: {{ batch.lesson.level }}/{{ batch.lesson.slug }}/{{ batch.lesson.n }}.

For **each** item, judge **each option in this sentence**, not in isolation. Use source evidence with IDs
`<source>:<id>` where source is `vesum`, `pravopys`, `textbook`, `grinchenko`, `sum20`, `vts`, or `ulif`.
Never use SUM-11 or a tool name as a source. Record at least one evidence ID for every judgement.

Set `requires_forced: false` if the sentence does not force **every** value in `requires`. Check every
form of the lemma, including forms outside the option list. Look for partitive genitive after request,
offer, or consumption verbs and mozhna ("may I?"); genitive of negation; animate accusative/genitive syncretism;
and any other alternative reading. Deny if an alternative reading fits, if a second option may be
correct, or if evidence is missing. Rewrite the item to force one reading or drop it; never repair an
unforced demand by removing a group from `requires`.

Return one YAML mapping with `answers`, one answer per question, exactly once and in option order.
Each answer has `activity`, `item`, `decision: confirm | deny`, non-empty `reason`,
`requires_forced: true | false`, and `options: [{text, judgement, evidence}]`.
Judgements are `valid`, `invalid`, or `depends_on_context`. Confirm only when the key is valid,
every distractor invalid, all judgements have evidence, and `requires_forced` is true.
An unsupported judgement may have empty evidence only in a deny with a reason starting `unresolved`.

